Package: cliqueR
Title: Lineage Tracing Analysis with the Clique Toolkit
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Aaron", "McKenna", email = "aaronatwpi@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: R interface to the clique Rust command-line tool for amplicon and
    UMI processing. Provides helpers for read-structure configuration, pipeline
    execution, BAM tag import, edit character matrices, lineage-tree
    reconstruction with in-process and external backends, and annotated tree
    visualization.
URL: https://github.com/aaronmck/clique
BugReports: https://github.com/aaronmck/clique/issues
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
SystemRequirements: clique (Rust binary, built from rust_cmd/); optional
    tree backends: IQ-TREE 2, VINE, PHYLIP MIX, and Python Cassiopeia
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    processx,
    rlang
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    withr,
    fs,
    tibble,
    dplyr,
    tidyr,
    readr,
    purrr,
    Matrix,
    ape,
    phangorn,
    Rsamtools,
    DropletUtils,
    ggtree,
    treeio,
    ggplot2,
    ggnewscale,
    reticulate,
    knitr,
    rmarkdown
Config/testthat/edition: 3
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
